Z||000000||WisconsinGT||02-20-2001||10:44 AM||||It is time for my Fiero to get a new steering wheel. Anyone know the color options for an 88GT. My wheel looks to be black. But I do not know if the color has worn off, or if black was an option. My interior color is gray. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ditz88GT||02-20-2001||02:26 PM||||My 88gt wheel is Black with a grey interior too.  Are you having it recovered or getting a new wheel altogether?  Here's why I'm asking, I was thinking of getting mine done in red leather insted of black and I was wondering what something like that might cost.  Anyway, just wanted to let you know that black is the color of mine too.||||reg||6
Z||000002||fropuff||02-20-2001||03:09 PM||||I think steering wheels are either black or saddle tan, not sure though.  I think all with gray interiors got the black; tan got the tan.||||reg||1
Z||000003||David Gamache||02-20-2001||11:34 PM||||I do the restration of leather steering wheels and the orginal colors for the 88 model year was a grayish black color that is no longer avaliable,and a beechwood tan that was a lighter shade than the earlier 84-87 brown. The orginal gray is so dark that when it begins to wear it appears to look black. The standard black is the current substitute color being used although a standard gray (lighter than orginal and closer to a standard dark gray is avaliable. I have also done special colors for customers such as red, white, and yellow with the shift knobs to match, so optional colors are avaliable but not generaly advertised. I also build GM style engine supports and sometimes deal in AC delco parts locally.  As you can imagine, fieros are one of my favorite hobbies like probably about everyone else on this great forum. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||02-21-2001||12:10 AM||||Actually, there are 3 shades of tan leather steering wheels.  '84-'85 are a dark brown (chocolate color), '86-'87 is a light tan and the '88 is beechwood (which is a more "orangish" color than the others).  <P>Also, there was never a black steering wheel offered from the factory. As previously stated, they turn black over time (the gray color wears off)......the tan ones do the same thing.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||02-21-2001||07:41 AM||||MrMike recovers them for $199, you'd have to ask him about colors though.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Loki||02-21-2001||09:58 AM||||OK, now that we have the colors down, how many steering wheel styles where there? Ive seen 3 so far...<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||02-21-2001||04:28 PM||||I have a 1984 SC with the tan interior.  It came with a brown steering wheel, but it is not leather.  The wheel has three flat slotted metal spokes that are painted painted black.  It think the wheel itself is a textured plastic or heavy vinyl with finger indetations molded onto the side facing away from the driver.<P>After all these years, the wheel still looks and feels like new.  It's not leather, but it also never leaks black goo.  <P>I have not seen a wheel like it on any other Fieros.  IMHO, it looks a lot better than the four spoke rectangular thing I have seen in most fieros.  <P> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||02-22-2001||01:58 AM||||Both my cars (84 SC and 86 GT) have the 3-spoke vinyl steering wheel.  I know the GT is supposed to have the leather, but the vinyl looks just as good and doesn't puke all over on hot days.  Actually, I think the vinyl looks better.  Just about every leather wheel I've seen has been twisted and wrinkled and horrible looking...||||reg||1
